## Non-blocking findings carried into implementation

- `_suppression_active` carries no docstring and gains two comparison semantics
  behind a flag. GH #447 exists because a docstring promised what its body did
  not do; the helper now documents both semantics.
- Doctrine section 10.5 described a suppression more durable than `check`
  provides, and the Phase 69 paragraph points at it. Section 10.5 rewritten to
  describe both modes.
- `isolate_gates_dir` did not patch `_workdir.root`, so the existing
  `check_session_total` tests would stat the real repository once the marker
  became load-bearing. Fixture extended, pinned to `tmp_path` exactly.

## What the PASS covers

Verified by reading or by tool: the K-window arithmetic and that `[-K]` indexes
`t[N-K+1]`; all four blocks of the inclusive-comparison table; that the new
keyword's default leaves every existing call site unaffected; the structural
`ts` guarantee; the T3/T4 discrimination matrix; blast radius; every checked
line citation.

Not verified by the reviewer, because it could not execute: the zero-and-zero
same-second corpus measurement, the probe outputs, and that the tests pass.

## Execution evidence produced at implementation

- T8's discriminating red observed at the intermediate commit: with anchor and
  filter landed but `inclusive` not passed, T8 failed alone while T1, T3 and T5
  were green.
- Anchor substitution against the working tree: `stamps[sig][0]` reddens T4 and
  only T4; `stamps[sig][-1]` reddens T3; the K-window floor passes both.
- The plan predicted T4 red before the fix and it was green, because today's
  never-suppress behaviour coincides with T4's expectation. The prediction was
  wrong and the anchor-substitution probe is what establishes T4's value.

